<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tamils</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tamil people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tamils are a people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-asia">South Asia</a> whose language, Tamil, has a literary tradition of more than two thousand years. Most live in the Indian state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a> and in northern and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, where a Tamil kingdom ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaffna">Jaffna</a> in the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, and a separate community descended from 19th-century plantation workers lives in Sri Lanka's central highlands. Large diasporas live in Malaysia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a> and elsewhere.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tamils.jpg" alt="Tamils" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hishampgm · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pongal_Festival.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
